# Fix: "should allow keyboard shortcut to open import dialog" Test

## Problem

The WebdriverIO test `import-dialog.spec.ts:77` fails with:
```
waitUntil condition timed out after 5000ms
```

The test expects Escape to close the dialog, but it doesn't.

## Root Cause

The app's Escape key handler (useKeyboardShortcuts.ts:114-121) only clears selection and tool state - it does NOT call `closeDialog()`.

```typescript
if (key === 'escape') {
  clearSelection();
  clearMergeStations();
  clearMeasure();
  setDrawFromStation(null);
  return;  // No closeDialog() call!
}
```

## Solution

### Two-Layer Fix (Belt and Suspenders)

1. **Global Escape Handler** (useKeyboardShortcuts.ts):
   - Check if `activeDialog` is set first
   - If yes, close dialog and return
   - Otherwise, clear selection/tool state as before

2. **Shared DialogWrapper Component**:
   - Create reusable component with Escape handling
   - Gate ALL close paths (Escape, backdrop, × button) through dirty check
   - Use app's existing confirm dialog pattern (not `window.confirm`)
   - Support flexible sizing via `size` prop
   - Use `useId()` for unique aria-labelledby IDs

### Key Decisions

| Decision | Choice |
|----------|--------|
| Architecture | Global handler + shared DialogWrapper (belt and suspenders) |
| Dirty confirmation | Use existing `ConfirmDialog` pattern (not `window.confirm`) |
| Close paths | ALL paths (Escape/backdrop/×) go through `requestClose()` |
| Sizing | `size` prop with presets (`sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`, `2xl`) |
| Event handling | Capture phase, check `event.repeat`, handle `'Esc'` key |
| aria-labelledby | Use `useId()` for unique IDs per dialog instance |

## Files to Change

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `src/components/Dialogs/DialogWrapper.tsx` | **Create** - Shared dialog wrapper |
| `src/hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.ts` | Add dialog close on Escape (before tool state clear) |
| `src/components/Dialogs/ImportDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper, remove local version |
| `src/components/Dialogs/DmpImportDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/NewProjectDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/ExportDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/ConfirmDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/OverwriteConfirmDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/UnsavedChangesDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/ErrorDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/EditShotDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/EditStationDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/EditSectionDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/DrawShotDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |
| `src/components/Dialogs/MergeDialog.tsx` | Use shared DialogWrapper |

## Implementation Details

### Global Escape Handler Fix (useKeyboardShortcuts.ts)

```typescript
// In handleKeyDown, BEFORE the existing Escape handling:
if (key === 'escape') {
  // First: close any open dialog
  const { activeDialog, closeDialog } = useUIStore.getState();
  if (activeDialog) {
    closeDialog();
    return;
  }

  // Then: clear selection/tool state (existing behavior)
  clearSelection();
  clearMergeStations();
  clearMeasure();
  setDrawFromStation(null);
  return;
}
```

### Shared DialogWrapper Component

```tsx
// src/components/Dialogs/DialogWrapper.tsx
import { useEffect, useId, ReactNode, useCallback } from 'react';
import { useUIStore } from '../../store/uiStore';

type DialogSize = 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' | 'xl' | '2xl' | '4xl' | '5xl';

const sizeClasses: Record<DialogSize, string> = {
  sm: 'max-w-sm',
  md: 'max-w-md',
  lg: 'max-w-lg',
  xl: 'max-w-xl',
  '2xl': 'max-w-2xl',
  '4xl': 'max-w-4xl',
  '5xl': 'max-w-5xl',
};

interface DialogWrapperProps {
  title: string;
  onClose: () => void;
  children: ReactNode;
  isDirty?: boolean;
  size?: DialogSize;
  'data-testid'?: string;
  maxHeight?: string;  // e.g., 'max-h-[90vh]' or 'max-h-[70vh]'
}

export function DialogWrapper({
  title,
  onClose,
  children,
  isDirty = false,
  size = '2xl',
  'data-testid': testId,
  maxHeight = 'max-h-[90vh]',
}: DialogWrapperProps) {
  const titleId = useId();
  const { openDialog: showConfirmDialog } = useUIStore();

  // Centralized close logic - ALL close paths go through here
  const requestClose = useCallback(() => {
    if (isDirty) {
      // Use app's existing confirm dialog pattern
      showConfirmDialog('unsaved-changes', {
        onConfirm: onClose,
      });
    } else {
      onClose();
    }
  }, [isDirty, onClose, showConfirmDialog]);

  useEffect(() => {
    const handleEscape = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
      // Handle both 'Escape' and legacy 'Esc'
      if ((e.key === 'Escape' || e.key === 'Esc') && !e.repeat && !e.defaultPrevented) {
        e.preventDefault();
        requestClose();
      }
    };

    // Use capture phase to handle before inner components
    document.addEventListener('keydown', handleEscape, true);
    return () => document.removeEventListener('keydown', handleEscape, true);
  }, [requestClose]);

  return (
    <div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center">
      {/* Backdrop - also goes through requestClose */}
      <div
        className="absolute inset-0 bg-black/50"
        onClick={requestClose}
      />

      {/* Dialog */}
      <div
        role="dialog"
        aria-modal="true"
        aria-labelledby={titleId}
        data-testid={testId}
        className={`relative bg-panel border border-border rounded-lg shadow-xl ${sizeClasses[size]} w-full mx-4 ${maxHeight} overflow-auto`}
      >
        {/* Header */}
        <div className="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 border-b border-border">
          <h2 id={titleId} className="text-lg font-medium">{title}</h2>
          <button
            onClick={requestClose}  // × button also goes through requestClose
            className="text-text-secondary hover:text-text-primary text-xl"
            aria-label="Close dialog"
          >
            ×
          </button>
        </div>

        {/* Content */}
        <div className="p-4">
          {children}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Migration Pattern for Each Dialog

```typescript
// Before (local DialogWrapper in each file):
function DialogWrapper({ title, onClose, children }) { ... }

// After:
import { DialogWrapper } from './DialogWrapper';

// Update usage:
<DialogWrapper
  title="Edit Section"
  onClose={closeDialog}
  size="4xl"  // Match existing sizing
  data-testid="edit-section-dialog"
  isDirty={formChanged}  // If dialog has form state
>
  {children}
</DialogWrapper>
```

### Dialog Sizing Migration Map

| Dialog | Current Width | New `size` Prop |
|--------|--------------|-----------------|
| ImportDialog | max-w-2xl | `"2xl"` |
| DmpImportDialog | max-w-2xl | `"2xl"` |
| NewProjectDialog | max-w-md | `"md"` |
| ExportDialog | max-w-2xl | `"2xl"` |
| ConfirmDialog | max-w-md | `"md"` |
| ErrorDialog | max-w-md | `"md"` |
| EditShotDialog | max-w-2xl | `"2xl"` |
| EditStationDialog | max-w-md | `"md"` |
| EditSectionDialog | max-w-5xl (wide) | `"5xl"` |
| DrawShotDialog | max-w-md | `"md"` |
| MergeDialog | max-w-md | `"md"` |

### Dialogs Requiring isDirty Support

| Dialog | Has Form State | isDirty Needed |
|--------|---------------|----------------|
| ImportDialog | Yes (shots, metadata) | Yes |
| DmpImportDialog | Yes (file path, section name) | Yes |
| NewProjectDialog | Yes (project name, location) | Yes |
| EditShotDialog | Yes (shot fields) | Yes |
| EditStationDialog | Yes (GPS coords) | Yes |
| EditSectionDialog | Yes (section metadata) | Yes |
| DrawShotDialog | Yes (shot fields) | Yes |
| ExportDialog | No (just selections) | No |
| ConfirmDialog | No | No |
| ErrorDialog | No | No |
| MergeDialog | No (just confirmation) | No |

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `useKeyboardShortcuts.ts` closes `activeDialog` on Escape before clearing tool state
- [ ] Shared `DialogWrapper` created at `src/components/Dialogs/DialogWrapper.tsx`
- [ ] DialogWrapper uses `useId()` for unique aria-labelledby
- [ ] DialogWrapper handles Escape with capture phase, checks `event.repeat`
- [ ] DialogWrapper accepts `'Esc'` key (legacy browsers)
- [ ] ALL close paths (Escape/backdrop/×) go through `requestClose()`
- [ ] Dirty dialogs show confirmation via existing `ConfirmDialog` pattern
- [ ] DialogWrapper supports flexible `size` prop
- [ ] All 13 dialogs migrated to shared DialogWrapper
- [ ] Dialog sizing preserved (no layout regressions)
- [ ] Test "should allow keyboard shortcut to open import dialog" passes
- [ ] All WebdriverIO tests pass
- [ ] Playwright tests unaffected
- [ ] Rust backend tests unaffected

